{
 "_comment": "Default of every config key. Source of truth for the options menu AND for the first-run ini: defaultsApply() sets these before configLoad(). A bare value applies to every platform; {\"switch\": n, \"pc\": n} per platform (a missing side = no default there); \"why\" is for people. After editing run tools_pc/gen_menudata.py. \"version\" is the ini's (Config.Version); a migration lists steps for inis older than its version: {\"key\",\"set\"|\"reset\",\"when\":{\"key\",\"eq\"}}. \"legacy\" keys are removed from the game but still read once, so a migration can look at them.",
 "version": 2,
 "migrations": [
  {
   "version": 1,
   "why": "Native widescreen and Widescreen auto FOV are gone: the picture always takes the output aspect. Whoever had the stretched 4:3 picture off (native widescreen off) gets forced 4:3 with bars. The fog form used to follow Visuals (Original = per-vertex): it is now its own key. The Custom gamepad layout is gone (Modern replaces it): a Custom seat (any player) falls back to 1.1 Jinx.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "key": "Video.AspectMode",
     "set": 1,
     "when": {
      "key": "Video.NativeWidescreen",
      "eq": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "key": "Video.PerPixelFog",
     "set": 0,
     "when": {
      "key": "Video.Visuals",
      "eq": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "key": "Input.PadPreset",
     "set": 0,
     "when": {
      "key": "Input.PadPreset",
      "eq": 3
     }
    },
    {
     "key": "Input.PadPreset2",
     "set": 0,
     "when": {
      "key": "Input.PadPreset2",
      "eq": 3
     }
    },
    {
     "key": "Input.PadPreset3",
     "set": 0,
     "when": {
      "key": "Input.PadPreset3",
      "eq": 3
     }
    },
    {
     "key": "Input.PadPreset4",
     "set": 0,
     "when": {
      "key": "Input.PadPreset4",
      "eq": 3
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": 2,
   "why": "Modern is a control style beside Enhanced and Original (Input.ControlScheme 2), no longer layout 5 of Input.PadPreset, and the style is per player like the layouts (Input.ControlScheme2..4). Players 2-4 take the old global style; a player on layout 5 becomes Modern with 1.1 Jinx as their Enhanced layout. Original ignored the layouts, so an Original player's layout goes back to 1.1 Jinx first.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "key": "Input.PadPreset",
     "set": 0,
     "when": {
      "key": "Input.ControlScheme",
      "eq": 1
     }
    },
    {
     "key": "Input.PadPreset2",
     "set": 0,
     "when": {
      "key": "Input.ControlScheme",
      "eq": 1
     }
    },
    {
     "key": "Input.PadPreset3",
